Description: film-fidelity Matrix-style digital rain for XScreenSaver
 MatrixCode is a standalone OpenGL/GLX XScreenSaver hack inspired by the
 original-era Matrix digital-rain aesthetic.
 .
 Its default profile uses an original clean-room glyph atlas, a fixed
 resolution-independent code grid, independently timed illumination waves,
 pale cursor cells, restrained optical glow and a lightweight 4:3 CRT display
 treatment. No film assets or third-party glyph textures are included.
